  <main>
    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-gray-900"><strong>Takes effect January 1, 2027.</strong> This is version 1.2 of the Service Provider Agreement. Until then, version 1.1 remains in effect: <a href="/legal/service-provider-agreement" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">read version 1.1</a>.</p>

        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Service Provider Agreement</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> January 1, 2027 <strong>Version:</strong> 1.2</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Service Provider Agreement ("Agreement") governs your use of the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Service Provider. Subject to §11, by listing services on the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Service Provider, you agree to be bound by this Agreement in addition to the BreederHQ Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and the Legal Definitions Schedule.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ is an introduction venue, not a party to your services.</strong> BreederHQ introduces Buyers, including animal owners who book services, to you. It does not negotiate, set, approve, guarantee, or enforce the price, terms, conditions, warranties, guarantees, health guarantees, deposits, reservation fees, refunds, scheduling, delivery or transport, or outcome of any agreement between you and a Buyer, and it is not a party to that agreement. You and the Buyer own your arrangement and every dispute about it. Sections 5.5 and 7A explain what this means for you.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This Agreement applies to Providers whose Services-related activity involves rendering services to animals or animal owners, including without limitation farriers, trainers, veterinarians, groomers, transporters, pet sitters, equine instructors, and other animal-care professionals (each, a "Service Provider").</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>A Service Provider account is for services only. You may not list, advertise, or offer any animal for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit through a Service Provider account, in any form.</strong> This covers puppies, kittens, litters, adult animals, livestock, and upcoming or expected litters, and it applies whether the animal is yours or someone else's. Animals are sold or placed on the Marketplace only by breeders, through a breeder account governed by the Breeder/Seller Agreement. If you both provide services and sell or place animals, you must use a breeder account for the animal sales and keep your Service Provider account to services. BreederHQ limits animal listings to breeder accounts so that they run under the controls that apply to them. A Service Provider account is not a way around those controls. See §3.6 and §9.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">"Service Provider," "you," and "your" refer in this Agreement to any individual or entity that lists services on the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Service Provider.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in this Agreement have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into this Agreement by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Eligibility and Qualifications</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 General Eligibility</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To list as a Service Provider on the BreederHQ Marketplace, you must:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Be at least 18 years of age (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction);</li><li>Have the legal authority and capacity to enter into this Agreement;</li><li>Provide accurate and truthful account and business information;</li><li>Maintain a valid mailing address and contact information within the BreederHQ service area;</li><li>Have the individual BreederHQ designates for your account pass the Identity Check described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service before any of your service listings is published, as set out in §2.5.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Professional Qualifications</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You represent and warrant that you hold all licenses, certifications, registrations, and qualifications required by applicable federal, state, and local law for the services you offer through the Services. <strong>You may not offer, advertise, or hold yourself out as authorized to perform any service through the Services for which you lack the required license, certification, registration, or qualification under applicable law.</strong> This includes (without limitation) state veterinary licensure for any service that constitutes the practice of veterinary medicine in the applicable jurisdiction, USDA licensure for any service that requires it, state transporter licensure where required, and any profession-specific certification that applicable law requires for the lawful rendering of the service.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.3 Insurance</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are responsible for maintaining all insurance coverage required by applicable federal, state, and local law for your operations, profession, and jurisdiction (including without limitation general liability, professional liability or errors-and-omissions, and worker's compensation where applicable). <strong>BreederHQ does not impose, require, evaluate, verify, hold, broker, or facilitate any insurance coverage. Your compliance with applicable insurance law is solely your independent legal responsibility.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.4 Documentation Requests</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may, in its sole discretion and from time to time, request from a Service Provider documentation supporting any representation the Service Provider has made on the Services, including without limitation representations of identity, business registration, professional license, certification, or accreditation. <strong>The Service Provider's submission of requested documentation is a condition of continued marketplace participation; it is not a representation that BreederHQ has reviewed, validated, evaluated, or accepted the documentation for any purpose other than the Service Provider's continued marketplace participation.</strong> BreederHQ does not open, read, validate, compare, or vouch for any documentation submitted under this section. Failure to provide requested documentation within a reasonable time may result in suspension or removal of the Service Provider's listings. Submission of documentation under this section does not give rise to any duty on BreederHQ's part to detect, investigate, or remedy any defect in the documentation, nor to monitor the documentation for subsequent expiration or change. A documentation request under this section, including one about a representation of identity, is separate from the Identity Check under §2.5: documentation submitted under this section does not satisfy or replace the Identity Check, and passing the Identity Check does not satisfy a documentation request.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.5 Identity Check</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">&gt; <strong>In plain terms:</strong> Before a service listing can be newly published on the Marketplace, one person must pass an ID check run by our identity provider (today, Stripe Identity), using a picture of a government-issued photo ID and a live selfie. There is no other way to meet this requirement: BreederHQ does not review ID documents itself or offer a manual review or other alternative. That person is your provider account's primary owner as shown in BreederHQ's records (normally the person who set the account up), even if others have been added to the account. Some service listings published before this requirement may remain public without a passed check unless BreederHQ withdraws them. BreederHQ will ask that person, not anyone else, to agree to the check before it starts. BreederHQ's systems receive the result, not the ID or selfie images. As soon as the result is recorded, BreederHQ has the images and identity details deleted from its Stripe account and keeps only whether the check passed, the check's reference number, and its date (a reason a check did not pass may also appear for a short time in BreederHQ's operational logs and error reports); anything Stripe itself keeps is governed by Stripe's own policies (the Privacy Policy explains this). BreederHQ does not currently charge Service Providers to publish service listings. Passing does not mean BreederHQ has checked you, your qualifications, or your services, and you may not say that it does. This box is a summary; the rest of this Section controls.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Passing the Identity Check described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service is a condition of publishing any service listing on the Marketplace. As of the effective date of this Agreement, the individual BreederHQ designates for your account (the "Designated Individual") is the account's owner (the "Account Owner"), as those terms are defined in the Legal Definitions Schedule. That individual must complete the Identity Check personally, using only their own genuine government-issued photo identification and their own live photo. BreederHQ may decline to publish, and may withdraw from public view, your service listings while this condition is not met, as provided in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. A service listing that was already public when this requirement first applied to you may remain public unless and until BreederHQ withdraws it under §2.6 of the Terms of Service; keeping it public is not a breach of this Agreement. The requirement applies to each service listing you publish after that time.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Consent of the Designated Individual.</strong> Before the Identity Check begins, BreederHQ will ask the Designated Individual to consent to it, including to the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider's collection and comparison of their identification document and live photo. That consent is the Designated Individual's own to give. Your acceptance of this Agreement does not give it on their behalf, and you may not give it for them or complete the Identity Check in their place. If the Designated Individual does not consent, does not complete the Identity Check, or does not pass it, the condition in this Section is not met. BreederHQ does not review identification documents itself and does not offer a manual review, accommodation alternative, or any other way to satisfy this condition. If the Designated Individual cannot or will not complete the Identity Check, for any reason, your service listings cannot be newly published on the Marketplace, and your remedy is the refund and cancellation described in the next paragraph.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Fees while the condition is not met.</strong> BreederHQ does not currently charge Service Providers a subscription or a fee to publish service listings (§6.2), so a service listing waiting on the Identity Check carries no listing fee. If you paid a Boost or promotion fee for a service listing that could not be published, or that BreederHQ withdraws from public view, because the condition in this Section is not met (including because the Designated Individual declines the Identity Check or cannot complete it), BreederHQ will, at your request through the contact in §13, refund the unused portion of that fee, calculated by day from the date of withdrawal or, for a listing that could not be published, from the date the Boost or promotion period began. If BreederHQ later introduces a subscription or listing fee for Service Providers under §6.2 and the condition in this Section is not met, you may cancel it for that reason by request through the contact in §13, and BreederHQ will end it on the date of your request and refund the unused portion of any prepaid term, calculated by day from that date. This paragraph does not apply if BreederHQ suspends or terminates your Marketplace access under §9 for fraud or misrepresentation in connection with the Identity Check.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Identity Check is performed by the Third-Party Identity Verification Provider, not by BreederHQ, and any display of its result on the Services is a Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough as described in §2.6 of the Terms of Service. <strong>Passing it is not BreederHQ's verification, vetting, approval, certification, or endorsement of you, your qualifications, or your services, and BreederHQ does not vouch for or guarantee any of them.</strong> It does not confirm any license, certification, insurance, or other qualification described in §§2.2 through 2.4. You may not state or imply, in your listings, communications with Buyers, or advertising on or off the Services, that BreederHQ has verified, vetted, approved, certified, or endorsed you or your services because the Identity Check was passed.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Listing Standards</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Service Description Accuracy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All listings must truthfully and accurately describe:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>The scope and nature of the services offered;</li><li>The methods, tools, equipment, and any animal-handling techniques used;</li><li>The species, breeds, or animal types served;</li><li>Any limitations on service (for example, animal size, behavior, medical condition);</li><li>The service location (Service Provider's facility, customer's location, mobile, or other);</li><li>The qualifications and experience of the individual(s) who will render the service.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Pricing Transparency</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All pricing must be clearly stated, in U.S. dollars unless otherwise specified, and must include or clearly disclose any additional fees (travel surcharges, after-hours fees, materials, etc.). You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Engage in bait-and-switch pricing (advertising one price, charging another);</li><li>Add undisclosed fees after a Buyer has committed to a service;</li><li>Misrepresent the basis for any fee (for example, characterizing a routine charge as an emergency surcharge).</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Service Area</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where you offer services in a specific geographic area, you must accurately represent that area. You may not list in service areas where you do not actually provide services for the purpose of search ranking or visibility.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Availability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where you display availability, calendar windows, or scheduling on the Services, you must keep that availability current. You may not display availability you cannot in fact provide.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.5 Cancellation and Refund Policy</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You must clearly publish your cancellation and refund policy before accepting any payment or booking. Your policy controls between you and the Buyer; BreederHQ does not set, adjudicate, or enforce your cancellation or refund policy.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.6 Prohibited Listings</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may NOT list:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Any animal for sale, placement, adoption for a fee, or deposit, or any upcoming or expected litter, in any form, whether in a listing, a profile, a service description, a photo, a message, or any other content on the Services. Listing animals from a Service Provider account is a violation of this Agreement. BreederHQ may remove the listing and may suspend or terminate your Marketplace access under §9, without limiting any other remedy. Animal sales and placements are made only by breeders through a breeder account under the Breeder/Seller Agreement;</li><li>Services you are not legally qualified or authorized to perform under applicable law;</li><li>Services involving the unlawful possession, transport, or treatment of any animal;</li><li>Services that violate the Acceptable Use Policy or any User Agreement;</li><li>Services using techniques, tools, or methods that constitute animal cruelty under applicable animal-welfare law;</li><li>Services that misrepresent the involvement, endorsement, or credentialing of any third party (including any breed registry, professional association, licensing authority, or accreditation body).</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Credential Attestations and Supporting Documentation</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A Service Provider's attestation of any professional credential, license, certification, accreditation, or registry status, and any document uploaded in support of such an attestation, is governed by §3.3 of the Terms of Service (Provider Attestations Regarding Credentials and Uploaded Documents) and §4.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy (Credential and Document Standards). The Service Provider reaffirms each of the representations and warranties set forth in those sections with respect to every Credential Attestation made on the Services.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Without limiting the foregoing: where the Service Provider attests to a credential issued by a body that maintains a Public Registry, and BreederHQ has implemented an integration with that Public Registry, BreederHQ may display a Third-Party Registry Passthrough indicator alongside the Service Provider's attestation under §2.5 of the Terms of Service. Where BreederHQ has not implemented an integration with the issuing body's Public Registry, the attestation is displayed as provider-attested only, without any Third-Party Registry Passthrough indicator. The Service Provider acknowledges that <strong>the absence of a Third-Party Registry Passthrough indicator does not imply that the Service Provider's credential is unverified, lapsed, or invalid; it reflects only that BreederHQ has not implemented a passthrough integration for the relevant issuing body.</strong></p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Standards of Service</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Standard of Care</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to perform all services rendered through the Services with the degree of skill, care, and judgment customarily exercised by a member of your profession practicing in your jurisdiction. Where your profession is governed by a published standard of practice promulgated by a professional association, licensing authority, or other recognized body, you agree to perform services in accordance with that standard.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Animal Handling</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree not to handle, treat, transport, or restrain any animal in a manner that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Constitutes neglect, abuse, or cruelty under applicable animal-welfare law;</li><li>Causes or is likely to cause unnecessary suffering, injury, or distress to the animal;</li><li>Disregards the animal's known medical or behavioral conditions where those conditions have been disclosed to you;</li><li>Violates any safety or handling guideline published by the relevant professional association.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Communication with Animal Owners</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Communicate clearly with the animal's owner regarding the scope, methods, timing, and pricing of services to be rendered;</li><li>Promptly notify the animal's owner of any injury, illness, adverse reaction, or material event affecting the animal that occurs during or as a result of the rendering of services;</li><li>Respond to Buyer inquiries and complaints, and to inquiries from BreederHQ, in a timely manner and in good faith;</li><li>Provide service records, treatment notes, or other documentation as requested by the animal's owner or as required by applicable law.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.4 Compliance with Applicable Law</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are solely responsible for complying with all applicable laws governing your profession and services, including without limitation:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>State veterinary practice acts and licensure requirements;</li><li>USDA licensing and inspection requirements (where applicable);</li><li>State and local business licensure and zoning requirements;</li><li>State and federal transportation regulations (where applicable);</li><li>Tax obligations that applicable law assigns to you, as set out in §10 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.5 Your Agreements with Buyers; No Duty to Mediate</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(a) You and the Buyer own your agreement.</strong> You and each Buyer decide every term of your arrangement, including price, deposit, scheduling, scope and methods of service, delivery or transport, cancellation and refund terms, and any guarantee, health guarantee, or warranty, and you are responsible to the Buyer for performing what you agree to. BreederHQ does not negotiate, set, review, approve, guarantee, or enforce any of those terms, does not perform or supervise your services, and is not a party to the arrangement. A listing, message, booking, invoice, payment request, or other feature of the Services that displays or records a term you set does not make that term BreederHQ's.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(b) Contract tools are tools.</strong> BreederHQ's contract templates, editing tools, AI-assisted conversion, and electronic signing are tools that BreederHQ supplies. You and the Buyer choose and own the contents of any Transaction Contract between you. A template, including a template BreederHQ provides, is a starting point; it is not legal advice, not a recommendation that any term suits your services, and not a term of BreederHQ's. BreederHQ does not become a party to a Transaction Contract by supplying the tools used to prepare, sign, store, or display it, as provided in §7C of the Terms of Service, and you are responsible for the content of any Transaction Contract you use as provided there.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>(c) No duty to mediate.</strong> BreederHQ has no duty to mediate, investigate, arbitrate, decide, or otherwise resolve any dispute between you and a Buyer or any other User. BreederHQ may choose, at its sole discretion, to help with a dispute, for example by passing along a message, providing records it holds, or acting on a report under the Acceptable Use Policy. Any such help is voluntary, may stop at any time, does not make BreederHQ a party to the dispute, and creates no obligation to help again or to reach any particular outcome. Action BreederHQ takes to enforce its own User Agreements, such as removing a listing or suspending an account, is not a decision of your dispute with a Buyer and does not affect your rights or the Buyer's rights against each other.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Pricing and Fees</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.1 Service Pricing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You have sole discretion over the pricing of your services. All prices must be listed in U.S. dollars unless otherwise specified.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.2 Platform Fees</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">By using the Marketplace, you agree to pay applicable BreederHQ platform fees. BreederHQ does not currently charge Service Providers a subscription, a fee to publish or keep a service listing on the Marketplace, or a commission on completed bookings. The platform fees BreederHQ currently charges Service Providers are:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Boost or promotion fees for featured listing placement, where you choose to buy them. Each is paid in advance for a fixed period and is not charged again automatically (if you turn on renewal, BreederHQ sends you a payment link when the period ends, and you are charged only if you pay it). Except as provided in §2.5 and in §9.2(b) of the Terms of Service (termination without cause), in the terms of a particular offer presented to you at purchase, or where applicable law requires otherwise, these fees are non-refundable, including when you unpublish the listing before the period ends.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Current prices are available on the BreederHQ website and at checkout. BreederHQ may change its prices and fees, or introduce a new fee (including a subscription, listing fee, or commission), only with at least thirty (30) days' notice by email to the address on file and by in-product notification. Before any recurring subscription is charged to you, the terms that will govern it (including its price, billing frequency, automatic renewal, how and when you may cancel, refunds, and what happens when it ends) will be set out in an update to this Agreement made under §11 and presented to you at checkout, and BreederHQ will ask for your affirmative consent to them.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If you also hold a separate breeder account as a Breeder/Seller Provider, that account's BreederHQ subscription and any listing subscription are governed by §4.2 of the Breeder/Seller Agreement.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.3 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payments from Buyers, where processed through the Services, are handled by our third-party payment processor. You agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Maintain a valid account with our payment processor in good standing;</li><li>Provide accurate banking and tax information for payouts;</li><li>Comply with the payment processor's terms of service and acceptable use policy;</li><li>Accept that payment processing fees are separate from BreederHQ platform fees.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ's own role in payments.</strong> BreederHQ's role in payments is limited to the following. (a) BreederHQ charges you, through its third-party payment processor, for any Boost, promotion, or other fee you buy from BreederHQ under §6.2; BreederHQ is the seller of what those charges pay for, and §6.2 governs them. (b) Where the Services let you request or accept payments from Buyers through your own account with the payment processor, BreederHQ supplies the software; the payment is made to you and processed by the payment processor under its terms. (c) Where a Buyer's payment is routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, BreederHQ acts only as your limited payments agent as described in §2.7 of the Terms of Service and §2.2 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms. In none of these roles does BreederHQ decide whether a payment, deposit, or refund is owed between you and a Buyer, hold funds in escrow or trust, or become a party to your arrangement with a Buyer.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.4 Payouts</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payouts to your connected bank account are processed according to the payout schedule established in your payment processor account. BreederHQ does not control payout timing, holds, or reserves imposed by the payment processor.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.5 Chargeback and Dispute Liability</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A payment for one of your transactions can result in a chargeback, reversal, payment dispute, or negative balance, whether the payment was made to your own account with the payment processor or was routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure on your behalf as described in §2.2 of the Marketplace Transaction Terms and §2.7 of the Terms of Service. Some of these can fall on BreederHQ's platform payment account, for example where a payment was routed that way or where the payment processor holds BreederHQ responsible for losses on your connected payment account. You acknowledge and agree that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li><strong>You are solely responsible</strong> for any chargebacks, reversals, payment disputes, or negative balances arising from your transactions, regardless of how the payment was routed;</li><li>If a chargeback or dispute results in a financial loss to BreederHQ's platform payment account, you agree to <strong>promptly reimburse BreederHQ</strong> for the full amount of such loss, including the original transaction amount, chargeback fees, payment processor penalties, and any related costs;</li><li>BreederHQ may recover amounts owed by deducting from your future payouts, debiting your connected payment account, setting off against other amounts owed to you, invoicing you directly, or pursuing collection activities or legal action;</li><li>You agree to <strong>cooperate fully</strong> with BreederHQ and the payment processor in responding to chargebacks and disputes;</li><li><strong>Failure to reimburse</strong> BreederHQ for chargeback losses within fifteen (15) days of notice may result in suspension or termination of your Marketplace access;</li><li>This obligation survives termination of this Agreement and your Marketplace account.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Indemnification</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To the fullest extent permitted by law, you agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless BreederHQ LLC, its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates (the "BreederHQ Parties") from and against any and all claims, demands, actions, damages, losses, liabilities, fines, penalties, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees), including those brought or asserted by a Buyer, another User, or a government authority, arising from or related to:</p>
